  "configuration_id": "config_046",
  "reason": "The current best (config_022: pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) achieves 0.635 acc / 0.618 F1. All completed experiments use PCA as the RNA encoder, leaving the RNA representation choice entirely unexplored. config_046 is a single-variable change from the current best, swapping pca_n2000 for scvi_n200 while holding image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (avgpool), fusion (weighted), and profile setting (multiprofile) constant. This directly tests whether a learned nonlinear RNA latent (scVI) captures biological structure that PCA misses, which is a critical design axis given that the RNA modality is the primary biological signal. If scvi_n200 improves performance, it identifies RNA encoder quality as a lever for further gains; if it does not, it confirms PCA sufficiency and redirects budget toward other dimensions (e.g., image encoder or fusion). This is the highest-information single experiment available under the limited budget."
}

